Record the messages a turn really contains. A user turn carrying both a
tool_result and text became one message with role `tool`, so the user's own text
was attributed to a tool; it is now split into the tool's response and the user
speaking. An assistant turn whose only block was an empty `TextBlock`, or a
`ThinkingBlock` the model signed but left blank, produced no parts at all and so
dropped out of both `gen_ai.output.messages` and the replayed history, leaving a
gap in the conversation. A block type this mapping has no part for is recorded
under the schema's content-type discriminator (`tool_result`) rather than the
Python class name (`ToolResultBlock`).

In streaming-input mode the caller's prompt is an async iterable that cannot be
read without starving the SDK, so the `invoke_agent` span had no input of its own;
it is now seeded from the user turn the CLI replays, which is the same text.
